--- a/AGENTS.md
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ Stage A semantics
+Stage A keeps the formal pipeline unchanged and uses internal scheduling modes A0_EXECUTION_READINESS, A1_DECISIVE_PILOT and A2_INDEPENDENT_GATE. A0 is non-claim-bearing; only A1 may create scientific observations. New assignment IDs do not reset topic-level engineering or redesign budgets.

--- a/rules/ROLE_MAINLINE.md
+++ b/rules/ROLE_MAINLINE.md
@@ Stage A dispatch
+Before dispatch, freeze a topic-level STAGEA_EXECUTION_READINESS_LEDGER. Across all assignments for the same topic, A0 has one initial round plus at most two engineering-correction batches and one legal same-object method redesign. Queue wait and hard external-blocker wait do not count as A0 execution rounds. Once A0 is READY, the next eligible action must be A1_DECISIVE_PILOT or an explicit blocker; no new static/preclaim successor may expand the packet. Budget exhaustion yields hold/blocker routing, never scientific STOP, and a new assignment does not reset the ledger.

--- a/rules/ROLE_CANDIDATE_OWNER.md
+++ b/rules/ROLE_CANDIDATE_OWNER.md
@@ Stage A minimum evidence
-Freeze 2-4 baselines and complete all listed evidence items as a uniform minimum.
+A1 requires one current strongest same-function baseline. Add at most one simple or attribution baseline only when needed to rule out ordinary tuning. Run 1-4 result-independent natural/formal cases. Complete atomic semantics on the minimal instance is mandatory; full workload matrices, platforms, statistics, complete baseline grids and full ablations belong to Stage B.

--- a/rules/ROLE_STAGEA_REVIEW.md
+++ b/rules/ROLE_STAGEA_REVIEW.md
@@ Required checks
+Treat one strongest fair baseline as the Stage A minimum. Reuse the frozen Stage 0 Q1/collision matrix and update only version drift, new collisions or claims affected by execution. Do not require Stage B evidence breadth for an A1 preliminary-support decision.

--- a/rules/AUTONOMOUS_SOFT_BLOCKER_RECOVERY.md
+++ b/rules/AUTONOMOUS_SOFT_BLOCKER_RECOVERY.md
@@ Scheduling
+The existence of another finite same-object route is insufficient after the topic cumulative Stage A budget is exhausted. Route to execution hold, external blocker, human reserve, or an explicitly user-approved exceptional continuation. Never reset the budget through a successor assignment.

